
<p>Bill Friskics-Warren for The New York Times:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>Her death was announced in a video posted on social media by her
nephew Bryan Seaver. No cause was provided. Concerns about Ms.
Parton’s health were raised last year as she <a href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/09/29/arts/music/dolly-parton-las-vegas.html">postponed</a>
and later canceled a Las Vegas residency, and intensified to the
point that she took to social media in October to announce, <a href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/10/08/arts/music/dolly-parton-health.html">“I
ain’t dead yet.”</a> This May, she said that she had responded
well to treatment after her immune and digestive systems had, as
she put it, “got all out of whack” in recent years.</p>

<p>From her hardscrabble beginnings to glittering stardom, Ms.
Parton’s life was the stuff of make-believe. With her voluptuous
figure, sparkly stage costumes and blond bouffant wigs, she was
likened by the writer Chet Flippo to the Big Rock Candy Mountain,
the Depression-era symbol of abundance. Her songs spoke to
millions, confronting privation and loss even as they radiated
possibility and hope.</p>

<p>She was, quintessentially, a uniter of people. In 2019, The New
York Times <a href="https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/21/arts/music/dolly-parton.html">ran a story</a> with the headline “Is There
Anything We Can All Agree On? Yes: Dolly Parton.”</p>
</blockquote>

<p><a href="https://www.threads.com/share/BANzyTBX7-/">Hillary Clinton, on Threads</a>:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>Dolly Parton did all the good she could, for all the people she
could, for as long as ever she could.</p>

<p>From her legendary songwriting to the Imagination Library — which
sent 1 million books a month to children across the country — she
was the best of America.</p>

<p>Dolly, we’ll miss your great heart.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>Parton accomplished so many great things, but man, the Imagination Library is just hard to believe. They’ve distributed over 330 million books to children — <em>and counting</em>. In lieu of flowers or anything else, her family is requesting that any money you might want to contribute to show your appreciation <a href="https://imaginationlibrary.com/">be donated to the library</a>. Count me in.</p>

